---
/**
 * The 5-day / 6-day work-week switch.
 *
 * Extracted because it is rendered twice — once in the desktop control bar and
 * once in the strip below the header that phones and tablets get. It used to
 * exist only inside `hidden lg:flex`, so below 1024px there was no way to
 * switch at all, and company-optimizer.astro tells the reader in plain English
 * to "switch the workweek control in the header to 6-day" — an instruction that
 * could not be followed on a phone.
 *
 * No ids: with two instances on the page they would collide. The group is named
 * with aria-label and the script finds the buttons by `.workweek-btn`, then
 * syncs every instance by `data-workweek` VALUE rather than by element
 * identity, so the two copies cannot end up disagreeing.
 */
---

<div
  role="group"
  aria-label="Work week length"
  class="flex items-center gap-0.5 bg-surface-sunken p-0.5 rounded-full border border-hairline shrink-0"
>
  <button
    type="button"
    data-workweek="5"
    aria-pressed="true"
    class="workweek-btn px-2.5 py-1 text-[0.6875rem] font-bold rounded-full cursor-pointer transition-colors"
    >5-day</button
  >
  <button
    type="button"
    data-workweek="6"
    aria-pressed="false"
    class="workweek-btn px-2.5 py-1 text-[0.6875rem] font-bold rounded-full cursor-pointer transition-colors"
    >6-day</button
  >
</div>
